#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mathieu_c

#% text
# `mathieu_c(a, q, z)` gives the even Mathieu function with characteristic value `a` and parameter `q`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is the even Floquet solution `ce_nu(z) = sum_k c_k cos((nu + 2k) z)` of `y'' + (a - 2 q cos(2 z)) y = 0` with `sum c_k^2 = 1` (DLMF 28.2, 28.12).

#% item
# Numerical values: Taylor series of the equation re-expanded along the segment from 0, and the normalization from the characteristic exponent `nu` (`cos(pi nu) = w_I(pi)`, DLMF 28.2.16) and the Fourier coefficients of the Floquet solution (continued fractions, `sum c_k^2 = 1`). Real `a` and `q` use this normalization throughout; complex `a` or `q` use the principal branches and may differ from other conventions by the normalization.

#% item
# `mathieu_c(a, 0, z) = cos(sqrt(a) z)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mathieu_c(2, 1, 3.2)
#% output
#= -0.8995311634414612

#% cell
n(mathieu_c(2, 1, 37/10), 20)
#% output
#= -0.7067473413037672704676

#% cell
mathieu_c(a, 0, z)
#% output
#= cos(z*a^(1/2))

#% text
# At a characteristic value the function is periodic:

#% cell
a0 = mathieu_characteristic_a(0, 1.0); mathieu_c(a0, 1.0, pi + 0.3) - mathieu_c(a0, 1.0, 0.3)
#% output
#= -3.3306690738754696e-16

